Reason: every frame each instance with a collision event copied every instance of each target object, sorted them by
object and id, and boxed them one by one, though almost every frame nothing touches. Each of Samus's shots is such an
instance (against the solids and every enemy), so shooting alone cost up to 1.7 ms a frame in collision dispatch in
Dolphin's emulated time (rm_a3a19 0.07 -> 1.81 ms). The pair tests change nothing, so the first hit can be looked for
anywhere: in the grid cells under self when they hold fewer instances than the target's bucket (clean instances are
in their cells; dirty ones are tested by their flag, and the grid is not synced, which would reorder cells for later
queries). With no hit the event is done; with one, the unchanged sorted walk starts at that hit, since every instance
before it misses. rm_a3a19's collision dispatch while firing: 1.81 -> 0.34 ms.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

